        "original_id": "b9e3ce85-87a6-5c03-aebf-2893f5590c2c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Baghdad ER, The Ten-Year Lunch: The Wit and Legend of the Algonquin Round Table, The Image\n- People: Matthew O'Neill, Jon Alpert, Dorothy Parker, Robert Benchley, George S. Kaufman, Edna Ferber, Marc Connelly, Harold Ross, Harpo Marx\n- Organizations: HBO, Algonquin Round Table\n- Places: New York City\n- Topics: Documentary films, Emmy Awards, Roaring Twenties\n\nFacts:\n- The Image premiered on HBO on January 27, 1990.\n- The Ten-Year Lunch: The Wit and Legend of the Algonquin Round Table is a 1987 American documentary film about the Algonquin Round Table.\n- The Algonquin Round Table was a floating group of writers and actors in the Roaring Twenties in New York City.\n- The Algonquin Round Table included Dorothy Parker, Robert Benchley, George S. Kaufman, Edna Ferber, Marc Connelly, Harold Ross, and Harpo Marx.\n- Baghdad ER is a documentary released by HBO on May 21, 2006.\n- Matthew O'Neill is a documentary filmmaker best known for his work on the HBO film Baghdad ER.\n- Matthew O'Neill and Jon Alpert won three Emmy Awards for Baghdad ER.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "75be276c-da95-5491-a37a-e65412616360",
        "text": "Page: Baghdad ER. Sentence: Baghdad ER is a documentary released by HBO on May 21, 2006.\nPage: The Ten-Year Lunch. Sentence: The Ten-Year Lunch: The Wit and Legend of the Algonquin Round Table is a 1987 American documentary film about the Algonquin Round Table, a floating group of writers and actors in the \"Roaring Twenties\" in New York City, which included great names such as Dorothy Parker, Robert Benchley, George S. Kaufman, Edna Ferber, Marc Connelly, Harold Ross and Harpo Marx.\nPage: Matthew O'Neill (filmmaker). Sentence: Matthew O'Neill is a documentary filmmaker best known for his work on the HBO film \"Baghdad ER\", for which he and co-creator Jon Alpert won three Emmy Awards.\nPage: The Image (1990 film). Sentence: The film premiered on HBO on January 27, 1990.",
